Minister Valerius Vane is a high-ranking member of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] and sits on the Calarian council. He is [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]]'s friend and former owner: Arctos says he was Vane's pet before the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] gave him speech and reason, that he saved Vane's life from a band of [[Org/RunGunners/index|RunGunners]], and that the two are equals now.

Vane's home is a gated three-story marble manor in the residential north of the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]], its walls carved with the family crest, a V with a sword through it. Its majordomo is [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley Hart]]. The Vane family keeps no [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] in the house, and holds that Hearts should not run all of society, though they still use them in their work.

In the manor's reading room hang two paintings, a small acrylic of a coastline and a long panorama of the Aurideon skyline. The panorama does not show the [[Pharos]], though the paint there is raised as if something had been painted over. Both are signed, and [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] copied the names down. Searching the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Masque District/Belvedere Library|Belvedere library]] found nothing for one name and, for the other, only a six-year-old clipping from a Vane family event, a photograph of the minister beside the artist and a line calling them one of the family's patronized artists.

The Party returned to the manor a second time and found Vane still at the council. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] left a note with [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] asking the minister to call at [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] when he had time.

Vane is about thirty-five, and [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] has served the family longer than Vane has been alive. He carries a small piece of palladium set near his heart, paired with a Palladium Rod kept in the manor, so that the household learns if his body is badly hurt. He keeps a couch in his office at the Templar Indictum for the nights he stays at the council.

When the Party came a third time, Vane was still away, and the council had been in an uproar for days over something that happened at a meeting. Arctos asked [[People/Crowley Hart|Crowley]] for the painting in the parlor, the long [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]] landscape of the Aurideon skyline. Crowley studied his face and said it was one of the minister's favourites, but that if Arctos truly needed it Vane would understand, and let them take it. Arctos also took two paintings of his own from his rooms. All three were carried to [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]] and left in the armory with [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Elias Ramsey|Elias]]. Arctos says he still means to ask Vane himself.
